    "q-132117": {
      "dom_id": "step-q132117",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14261478/assets/6dab892083ee6c9d0e77462cf2e5cf0f667e43b9c5ceb09aa4f6386d6e2f0c79.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y={x}^{3}$ and $y=\\sqrt[3]{x},$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14261478/assets/8df9c4544478d7146dbcb1790c8ed9a9f57cd1e52b1f50a8b344c2aa0551fa90.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le \\sqrt[3]{x}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{\\sqrt[3]{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{\\sqrt[3]{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-132117-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{x}}^{{x}^{3}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx",
